From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 15:55:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 008/117] dt-bindings: dma: Apple SIO

Apple SmartIO is a firmware-backed I/O coprocessor used by T8010 to move
peripheral data.  It exposes an A7IOP register window, a shim register
window, four mailbox interrupts and endpoint-addressed DMA channels.

Describe the firmware, power-domain and interrupt resources shared by the
SmartIO core and its DMA provider.  Use one DMA cell for the endpoint ID;
the first supported client is the SPI3 transmit endpoint.

The binding describes the complete coprocessor rather than a touchscreen
protocol.  SIO core and DMA engine implementations follow in separate
commits.  The schema passes dt-doc-validate and the complete stack was
boot-tested on J172 while uploading the touch firmware through SmartIO.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: f5bbfb9da37efab473f998cea35f280fa9907d48
